Date:   Fri Aug 14 22:19:41 2026 -0700

    feat: report explain's source view in the JSON answer

    #99 made `explain` say which tree it read, but only in the text header.
    ExplainResponse carried no provenance, so `explain --head --format json`
    and `explain --format json` were byte-identical on a clean tree and a
    machine consumer could not tell which tree the declarations described.

    Adds commit / tree / worktree_snapshot, the same field names and
    semantics def, neighbors and impact already expose (schema 1.x is
    additive-only, so new optional fields are in contract). The text header
    and the JSON fields are now computed from one expression, so the two
    renderings cannot disagree about the tree they read.

